      "writtenOn": "2022-08-11T19:17:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The prebuilt clang/llvm libraries have changed locations\nand might be changed again. So symlinks are used.\nCopying without preserving symlink in the out directory\nseems to be a safer way to be backward compatible.\nIt would be better to have a solution now that can work \nwith and without syminks.\n\nTo copy and preserve symlinks, the destination files \nwill need to be copied before we can execute: \n  cp -d ... \u0026\u0026 chmod ... \nIs there any existing .go or ninja build rule that can\nrecursively follow and copy symlink destinations?\nIs there a way to find which callers of CpExecutable\nneed to preserve symlinks?\n\nIf that can be identified, maybe we can\nadd another version of CpExecutable\nthat do not preserve symlink\nand use it to fix b/241815504.",
      "parentUuid": "50758cda_cd37eea6",
